{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates the variance of each lottery and prefers the one with higher variance. Variance can be calculated from the outcomes and their probabilities. For Lottery A: outcomes are 2500 (33%) and 0 (67%); for Lottery B: outcomes are 2400 (34%) and 0 (66%). The variance of a lottery is computed as E[X²] - (E[X])². Both lotteries have two outcomes, so variance is computable. Therefore, the decision reason is applicable to this decision problem.",
